00:06:54.373 --> 00:06:55.624
I'm just gonna be here.

00:06:57.793 --> 00:06:59.878
Peter, I don't think we need

00:06:57.793 --> 00:06:59.878
a donkey for this climb.

00:06:59.920 --> 00:07:01.922
Of course we don't

00:06:59.920 --> 00:07:01.922
<i>need</i> a donkey, Lois.

00:07:01.964 --> 00:07:02.965
It's a status thing here.

00:07:03.007 --> 00:07:04.383
You, leather man.

00:07:04.508 --> 00:07:05.717
You sell me donkey.

00:07:18.939 --> 00:07:20.941
I don't know what it is,

00:07:20.983 --> 00:07:24.611
but you... have got... it.

00:07:28.949 --> 00:07:30.951
(all gasp)

00:07:41.003 --> 00:07:43.172
Oh, my God.

00:07:43.214 --> 00:07:44.965
It's enormous.

00:07:45.007 --> 00:07:46.967
Lois, this is probably a

00:07:45.007 --> 00:07:46.967
terrible time to remember this,

00:07:47.009 --> 00:07:49.011
but I think I might have

00:07:47.009 --> 00:07:49.011
left the weed whacker on.

00:07:49.053 --> 00:07:51.180
(engine revving)

00:07:55.684 --> 00:07:57.186
Well, look who's here.

00:07:57.228 --> 00:07:58.937
I didn't believe you'd actually

00:07:57.228 --> 00:07:58.937
follow through with this.

00:07:58.979 --> 00:08:00.605
Oh, hey, Fishman.

00:08:00.647 --> 00:08:02.400
Hey, listen, on

00:08:00.647 --> 00:08:02.400
a scale of one to ten,

00:08:02.441 --> 00:08:04.443
how bad is the bathroom

00:08:02.441 --> 00:08:04.443
situation up here?

00:08:04.568 --> 00:08:06.570
Like, ten is a suite

00:08:04.568 --> 00:08:06.570
at the Four Seasons,

00:08:06.611 --> 00:08:08.572
and one is

00:08:06.611 --> 00:08:08.572
a tied-up raincoat sleeve

00:08:08.613 --> 00:08:09.823
at a party in your honor.

00:08:09.865 --> 00:08:11.242
Yes, we're here, Ross.

00:08:11.283 --> 00:08:13.369
When our family says that

00:08:11.283 --> 00:08:13.369
we're gonna do something,

00:08:13.411 --> 00:08:14.661
we follow through

00:08:13.411 --> 00:08:14.661
with it.

00:08:14.703 --> 00:08:16.997
Yeah, in fact, not only

00:08:14.703 --> 00:08:16.997
are we gonna climb it,

00:08:17.039 --> 00:08:18.999
we are gonna beat

00:08:17.039 --> 00:08:18.999
you guys to the top.

00:08:19.041 --> 00:08:20.000
(chuckles)

00:08:20.042 --> 00:08:20.959
I seriously

00:08:20.042 --> 00:08:20.959
doubt that.

00:08:21.001 --> 00:08:23.045
Oh, yeah?

00:08:21.001 --> 00:08:23.045
Well, so do I!

00:08:23.087 --> 00:08:24.380
Yeah, so you watch it, Fishman.

00:08:24.422 --> 00:08:26.257
We are gonna beat you so bad,

00:08:26.298 --> 00:08:28.592
you'll think you gave

00:08:26.298 --> 00:08:28.592
Chris Brown an STD.

00:08:28.633 --> 00:08:29.676
Is that what happened?

00:08:29.718 --> 00:08:31.262
You're not gonna

00:08:29.718 --> 00:08:31.262
beat us to the top.

00:08:31.303 --> 00:08:34.014
In fact, you probably won't

00:08:31.303 --> 00:08:34.014
even climb Everest at all.

00:08:34.056 --> 00:08:34.890
You don't have the nerve.

00:08:34.932 --> 00:08:35.974
Like hell I don't.

00:08:36.016 --> 00:08:37.684
Getting to the top

00:08:36.016 --> 00:08:37.684
ahead of you

00:08:37.726 --> 00:08:39.978
is gonna be one of the

00:08:37.726 --> 00:08:39.978
greatest moments of my life.

00:08:40.020 --> 00:08:42.689
It might even beat graduating

00:08:40.020 --> 00:08:42.689
from chiropractor school.

00:08:42.731 --> 00:08:44.108
Robert Baker.

00:08:46.026 --> 00:08:48.028
Brad O'Bannon.

00:08:49.029 --> 00:08:51.031
Anyone.

00:08:56.745 --> 00:08:58.497
Okay, the Fishmans are

00:08:56.745 --> 00:08:58.497
heading up the North Face,

00:08:58.622 --> 00:09:00.040
but I've been studying

00:08:58.622 --> 00:09:00.040
this map

00:09:00.082 --> 00:09:01.875
and I think we've got a better

00:09:00.082 --> 00:09:01.875
chance of beating them

00:09:01.917 --> 00:09:03.043
if we go

00:09:01.917 --> 00:09:03.043
up the South Face.

00:09:03.085 --> 00:09:04.669
Oh, we don't need

00:09:03.085 --> 00:09:04.669
a map, Brian.

00:09:04.711 --> 00:09:06.630
I got us a GPMS machine.

00:09:06.671 --> 00:09:07.923
Go up.

00:09:06.671 --> 00:09:07.923
WOMAN (annoyed):

00:09:07.965 --> 00:09:09.049
Just go up.

00:09:07.965 --> 00:09:09.049
What do you think?

00:09:09.091 --> 00:09:10.926
Sorry.

00:09:10.968 --> 00:09:13.053
just stop freaking out

00:09:10.968 --> 00:09:13.053
Okay, can everyone

00:09:13.095 --> 00:09:14.638
like, two minutes?

00:09:13.095 --> 00:09:14.638
and just give me,

00:09:14.679 --> 00:09:16.640
God!

00:09:16.681 --> 00:09:19.017
Everyone's always yelling at me.

00:09:16.681 --> 00:09:19.017
(crying):

00:09:19.059 --> 00:09:20.685
W... All the questions!

00:09:20.727 --> 00:09:22.480
All right, well, maybe

00:09:20.727 --> 00:09:22.480
we'll turn you on later

00:09:22.521 --> 00:09:23.897
and see how you feel.

00:09:23.939 --> 00:09:25.941
She was so nice

00:09:23.939 --> 00:09:25.941
in the store.

00:09:25.983 --> 00:09:28.277
Well, come on, everyone,

00:09:25.983 --> 00:09:28.277
let's get started.

00:09:33.907 --> 00:09:35.909
(shuddering)

00:09:36.910 --> 00:09:38.912
Brian, I'm not sure

00:09:36.910 --> 00:09:38.912
I can do this.

00:09:38.954 --> 00:09:41.915
It's chillier out here

00:09:38.954 --> 00:09:41.915
than Angelina Jolie.

00:09:41.957 --> 00:09:43.083
Something like that.

00:09:43.125 --> 00:09:45.085
I-I-I don't know,

00:09:43.125 --> 00:09:45.085
I-I-I'm so cold.

00:09:45.127 --> 00:09:47.546
She took that sad

00:09:45.127 --> 00:09:47.546
old lady's husband.

00:09:47.671 --> 00:09:49.673
You're just gonna have to

00:09:47.671 --> 00:09:49.673
block out the cold, Stewie.

00:09:49.714 --> 00:09:51.342
Picture yourself

00:09:49.714 --> 00:09:51.342
in a warm place.

00:09:51.383 --> 00:09:52.301
(breathes deeply)

00:09:52.343 --> 00:09:53.969
Okay, I think I can do that.

