00:15:47.322 --> 00:15:48.824
Didn't I tell you

00:15:47.322 --> 00:15:48.824
to bring trail mix?

00:15:48.866 --> 00:15:50.492
Yeah, but by that

00:15:48.866 --> 00:15:50.492
I thought you meant

00:15:50.534 --> 00:15:54.245
a set list of totally awesome

00:15:50.534 --> 00:15:54.245
tunes, which I do have.

00:15:54.287 --> 00:15:56.331
♪ I got the power! ♪

00:15:56.373 --> 00:15:58.458
And after this, it's

00:15:56.373 --> 00:15:58.458
"Everybody Dance Now"

00:15:58.500 --> 00:16:00.293
and after that, it's

00:15:58.500 --> 00:16:00.293
"Come Baby Come."

00:16:00.335 --> 00:16:01.837
That sounds

00:16:00.335 --> 00:16:01.837
like<i> Jock Jams.</i>

00:16:01.879 --> 00:16:04.840
It is similar

00:16:01.879 --> 00:16:04.840
to<i> Jock Jams.</i>

00:16:04.882 --> 00:16:06.257
It is<i> Jock Jams.</i>

00:16:11.555 --> 00:16:14.349
You guys, look,

00:16:11.555 --> 00:16:14.349
there's something up ahead.

00:16:16.100 --> 00:16:17.310
I think it's a person.

00:16:17.352 --> 00:16:19.312
Oh, my God,

00:16:17.352 --> 00:16:19.312
maybe they have food.

00:16:19.354 --> 00:16:21.356
Maybe it's a rescue team.

00:16:32.534 --> 00:16:34.745
Oh, my God,

00:16:32.534 --> 00:16:34.745
it's Ben Fishman.

00:16:35.787 --> 00:16:36.872
Is he...?

00:16:36.914 --> 00:16:38.498
Yep. He's dead.

00:16:38.540 --> 00:16:40.458
Oh, great. Not only are we

00:16:38.540 --> 00:16:40.458
caught in this blizzard,

00:16:40.500 --> 00:16:43.086
but there's some maniac up here

00:16:40.500 --> 00:16:43.086
freezing people to death.

00:16:43.127 --> 00:16:44.713
That poor boy.

00:16:44.755 --> 00:16:47.674
We should bury him.

00:16:44.755 --> 00:16:47.674
It's only right.

00:16:47.716 --> 00:16:50.093
Yeah, yeah, we should, Lois.

00:16:47.716 --> 00:16:50.093
You're right.

00:16:50.134 --> 00:16:52.679
Or we could...

00:16:52.721 --> 00:16:53.722
Could what?

00:16:53.764 --> 00:16:55.098
Eat him.

00:16:55.139 --> 00:16:56.683
(all gasp)

00:16:55.139 --> 00:16:56.683
Brian!

00:16:56.725 --> 00:16:59.352
Look, if we don't eat something

00:16:56.725 --> 00:16:59.352
soon, we're all gonna pass out

00:16:59.394 --> 00:17:01.396
from exhaustion and freeze

00:16:59.394 --> 00:17:01.396
to death just like him.

00:17:02.940 --> 00:17:04.691
Are we really

00:17:02.940 --> 00:17:04.691
considering this?

00:17:04.733 --> 00:17:06.526
We're talking

00:17:04.733 --> 00:17:06.526
about eating a person.

00:17:06.568 --> 00:17:08.779
Yeah, I'm not so sure

00:17:06.568 --> 00:17:08.779
about this.

00:17:11.531 --> 00:17:12.699
Oh, I thought

00:17:11.531 --> 00:17:12.699
we decided.

00:17:12.741 --> 00:17:13.784
I'm sorry.

00:17:13.825 --> 00:17:18.329
Well... I guess

00:17:13.825 --> 00:17:18.329
we don't have a choice.

00:17:22.584 --> 00:17:25.420
I am oddly prepared for this.

00:17:27.965 --> 00:17:29.591
Oh, God, Peter.

00:17:29.633 --> 00:17:32.010
I hope Ben would forgive

00:17:29.633 --> 00:17:32.010
us for what we did.

00:17:32.135 --> 00:17:35.513
Look, we needed to eat,

00:17:32.135 --> 00:17:35.513
the same way birds need to fly.

00:17:35.555 --> 00:17:37.808
What do you mean, you don't have

00:17:35.555 --> 00:17:37.808
our names on there?

00:17:37.849 --> 00:17:40.184
My wife and I absolutely have

00:17:37.849 --> 00:17:40.184
to be on this flight.

00:17:40.226 --> 00:17:41.728
I'm doing the best

00:17:40.226 --> 00:17:41.728
I can, sir.

00:17:41.770 --> 00:17:43.438
Do you have

00:17:41.770 --> 00:17:43.438
your confirmation number?

00:17:43.480 --> 00:17:46.566
I think you'll find all the

00:17:43.480 --> 00:17:46.566
information you need on here.

00:17:46.608 --> 00:17:48.192
Sir, this is just

00:17:46.608 --> 00:17:48.192
a piece of paper

00:17:48.234 --> 00:17:50.779
with the word "south"

00:17:48.234 --> 00:17:50.779
written on it.

00:17:50.821 --> 00:17:52.614
Can I speak to your supervisor?

00:17:52.656 --> 00:17:55.366
You guys, there's

00:17:52.656 --> 00:17:55.366
someone up ahead.

00:17:57.619 --> 00:17:58.620
Ben?!

00:17:58.662 --> 00:18:00.246
Ben?!

00:18:00.288 --> 00:18:02.165
Oh, my God, it's

00:18:00.288 --> 00:18:02.165
the Fishmans.

00:18:02.206 --> 00:18:03.625
They look terrible.

00:18:03.667 --> 00:18:05.627
(wearily):

00:18:03.667 --> 00:18:05.627
Have you seen Ben?

00:18:05.669 --> 00:18:07.629
We lost him

00:18:05.669 --> 00:18:07.629
in the storm.

00:18:07.671 --> 00:18:09.464
We're headed back up

00:18:07.671 --> 00:18:09.464
to find him.

00:18:09.506 --> 00:18:11.758
I just hope he's not trapped

00:18:09.506 --> 00:18:11.758
in some crevice somewhere.

00:18:11.800 --> 00:18:14.469
Well, my gut tells me

00:18:11.800 --> 00:18:14.469
he'll be squeezing himself out

00:18:14.511 --> 00:18:15.804
of a crevice very soon.

00:18:23.645 --> 00:18:26.606
Oh! We finally made

00:18:23.645 --> 00:18:26.606
it below the storm.

00:18:26.648 --> 00:18:28.775
Look! I see base camp!

00:18:28.817 --> 00:18:31.486
Yay!

00:18:28.817 --> 00:18:31.486
We're gonna be okay!

00:18:34.656 --> 00:18:36.240
(thunder crashing)

00:18:37.617 --> 00:18:41.204
Wait! We have to go back.

00:18:41.245 --> 00:18:43.040
What? What are you

00:18:41.245 --> 00:18:43.040
talking about?

00:18:43.081 --> 00:18:45.291
Kids, your mom is clearly

00:18:43.081 --> 00:18:45.291
delirious from the altitude.

00:18:45.333 --> 00:18:47.418
I say we leave her

00:18:45.333 --> 00:18:47.418
behind and marry

00:18:47.460 --> 00:18:49.253
that hot new assistant

00:18:47.460 --> 00:18:49.253
from my work.

00:18:49.295 --> 00:18:50.839
Look, Ben freezing to

00:18:49.295 --> 00:18:50.839
death was one thing.

00:18:50.881 --> 00:18:53.008
We had nothing

00:18:50.881 --> 00:18:53.008
to do with that.

00:18:53.050 --> 00:18:55.593
But we just let Ross and

00:18:53.050 --> 00:18:55.593
Pam walk back up there,

00:18:55.635 --> 00:18:57.428
probably to

00:18:55.635 --> 00:18:57.428
their deaths.

00:18:57.470 --> 00:18:59.597
And you know what?

00:18:57.470 --> 00:18:59.597
That's not who we are.

00:18:59.639 --> 00:19:01.850
We're the Griffins.

00:18:59.639 --> 00:19:01.850
And you know how we win?

00:19:01.892 --> 00:19:04.602
You know how we keep

00:19:01.892 --> 00:19:04.602
from being second-best?

00:19:04.644 --> 00:19:05.896
We do the right thing.

00:19:05.937 --> 00:19:08.648
We go back up there

00:19:05.937 --> 00:19:08.648
and save them.

00:19:08.690 --> 00:19:11.609
Tell me again why we ate

00:19:08.690 --> 00:19:11.609
a person before we ate the dog.

00:19:11.651 --> 00:19:13.028
(sighs) Your mom's right.

00:19:13.070 --> 00:19:16.114
Let's head

00:19:13.070 --> 00:19:16.114
back up there.

00:19:16.239 --> 00:19:17.615
Plus, if we don't rescue

00:19:16.239 --> 00:19:17.615
the Fishmans,

00:19:17.657 --> 00:19:19.534
their Jewish god is

00:19:17.657 --> 00:19:19.534
just gonna sit there

00:19:19.576 --> 00:19:21.036
and make us feel guilty.

00:19:21.078 --> 00:19:24.497
You do... whatever you want.

00:19:27.667 --> 00:19:29.502
(sniffing)

00:19:29.544 --> 00:19:31.337
Over here!

00:19:29.544 --> 00:19:31.337
I think I smell 'em!

00:19:35.717 --> 00:19:39.096
Oh, my God!

00:19:35.717 --> 00:19:39.096
Look down there!

00:19:41.765 --> 00:19:44.559
We got to get them out!

00:19:41.765 --> 00:19:44.559
They'll die down there!

00:19:44.601 --> 00:19:46.269
Well, we've got some rope.

00:19:46.310 --> 00:19:47.854
(ice cracking)

00:19:47.896 --> 00:19:49.522
Quick, Peter!

00:19:49.564 --> 00:19:51.566
You're the only one strong

00:19:49.564 --> 00:19:51.566
enough to carry two people.

00:20:03.536 --> 00:20:04.579
(gasping)

00:20:10.961 --> 00:20:12.503
(grunting)

00:20:16.716 --> 00:20:18.676
All right, I got 'em!

00:20:16.716 --> 00:20:18.676
Pull me up!

00:20:18.718 --> 00:20:21.721
(all grunting)

00:20:21.763 --> 00:20:23.765
Peter, we can't do it!

00:20:23.807 --> 00:20:25.142
You're too heavy!

00:20:25.183 --> 00:20:26.559
Keep going!

00:20:25.183 --> 00:20:26.559
You're almost there!

00:20:31.148 --> 00:20:33.524
I found a rock I like.

00:20:36.945 --> 00:20:38.947
Griffins, I don't know

00:20:36.945 --> 00:20:38.947
how to thank you.

00:20:38.989 --> 00:20:40.782
We never would have made it

00:20:38.989 --> 00:20:40.782
without your help.

00:20:40.824 --> 00:20:42.700
Oh, you would've done

00:20:40.824 --> 00:20:42.700
the same for us.

00:20:42.742 --> 00:20:45.578
There are more

00:20:42.742 --> 00:20:45.578
important things

00:20:42.742 --> 00:20:45.578
than a petty rivalry.

00:20:45.620 --> 00:20:47.747
We're just happy

00:20:45.620 --> 00:20:47.747
that you're okay.

00:20:47.789 --> 00:20:50.708
PAM:

00:20:47.789 --> 00:20:50.708
Well, thank you both.

00:20:47.789 --> 00:20:50.708
You saved our lives.

00:20:50.750 --> 00:20:54.754
And Peter, I'll never

00:20:50.750 --> 00:20:54.754
forget what you did for

00:20:50.750 --> 00:20:54.754
us. You're a good man.

00:20:54.796 --> 00:20:58.466
All right, you rest

00:20:54.796 --> 00:20:58.466
up, get better, we ate

00:20:54.796 --> 00:20:58.466
your son. Bring it up!